-- title:
--   Nonzero elements of the isogeny subring come from isogeny data
-- statement:
--   Let $F$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $0$ and $W$ an affine Weierstrass curve over $F$ that is elliptic, equipped with the three interface assumptions of the project: a bijection between $W.\mathrm{Point}$ and the places of $W.\mathrm{FunctionField}$ over $F$ under which every place has degree $1$ (`GenusOnePlaceGate`), the centring condition that at the place attached to a nonsingular affine point $(x,y)$ both coordinate classes $X$ and $Y-y$ lie in the nonunits of the associated valuation subring (`GenusOnePlaceGate.IsCentred`), and Abel's theorem in the form that a divisor of degree $0$ is principal exactly when its sum in $W.\mathrm{Point}$ vanishes (`AbelTheorem`). Assume $hNs$: for every isogeny endomorphism datum $D$ on $W$ — an $F$-algebra endomorphism $\iota$ of $W.\mathrm{FunctionField}$ that is integral and makes the function field finite over itself along $\iota$ — the push-forward norm formula holds along $\iota$, i.e. for every nonzero $f$ and every divisor cut out by $\operatorname{ord}(f)$, the push-forward of that divisor at a place $v$ equals $v.\mathrm{ord}$ of the algebra norm of $f$. Then for every additive endomorphism $\psi$ of $W.\mathrm{Point}$ lying in the subring of $\mathrm{AddMonoid.End}\,W.\mathrm{Point}$ generated by the endomorphisms $D.\mathrm{pointEnd}$ (the transport of the $\mathrm{Pic}^0$ push-forward along $\iota$ through the genus-one isomorphism $W.\mathrm{Point}\cong\mathrm{Pic}^0$), and with $\psi\neq 0$, there exists a datum $D$ with $D.\mathrm{pointEnd}=\psi$.
--
--   This is the statement that the ring generated by isogeny-induced endomorphisms of the group of points adds nothing new: apart from $0$, every element of it is again induced by a single isogeny datum, the function-field counterpart of the classical fact that $\operatorname{End}(E)$ consists of $0$ together with the isogenies $E\to E$. It is used to transfer degree and norm computations to arbitrary nonzero elements of the endomorphism ring, in particular in the results bounding traces and degrees by a quadratic form and in the identification of kernels of point maps attached to curves with equal $j$-invariant.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_WeierstrassCurve_Affine_IsogenyEndDatum_exists_pointEnd_eq_of_mem_isogenyEndSubring.lean

import Mathlib
